  "about": "Held document salma__03: its protocol line is labelled although the record is not attached. Revised 7 Nov 2026 (oncologist audit): quote-only facts for stage, margins, marker and mismatch-repair result rows, imaging and pathologist impressions, addendum text and the regimen line were labelled by reading each document (a regimen already on its cycle record is not a separate fact); the urea cream on returning__06 was missing from the gold. Hand-authored gold for the HELD-OUT documents in data/eval/heldout (written from the document definitions in scripts/demo-docs/heldout-docs.ts, same rules as data/eval/gold.json). One entry per fact a records officer would list, restricted to PRD §7.2 event types. `date` = the event's own date (YYYY-MM-DD); `match` = text that must appear in the extracted quote or fields (case-insensitive). Prescriptions and discharge medication lists: one entry per medication. A study or specimen the document only refers to is listed when the document gives it its own date or says its report is awaited. Courses of treatment with a start and an end (radiotherapy) carry no date in the gold (the event date is ambiguous). Bills carry no clinical events. Handwritten prescriptions list none (never auto-extracted). `identity` is the expected header decision against the patient in patients.json (a handwritten header is `insufficient` and held, as in gold.json); `held` = the document must not reach the record without a person's decision.",
